{"id": 33, "ts": 1780419555.2787573, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James and Emily\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strong stress resilience and technical aptitude\u2014handling stress well, being very conscientious, and having excellent weather\u2011assessment and computer skills are indeed valuable for long\u2011haul operations. However, the same notes also flag B as \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative,\u201d which directly undermine crew cooperation and professional communication, both non\u2011negotiable for safe, sustained international flights.\nCandidate\u202fC, while noted to have some communication challenges and a self\u2011focused style, is described as 100\u202f% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, and consistently creates a positive atmosphere with the crew. Reliability and a constructive cockpit environment are foundational for long\u2011distance missions, and C\u2019s decision\u2011making speed offsets the modest communication drawback.\nGiven that B\u2019s attitude issues could jeopardize crew coordination under fatigue, I am less convinced B is the safer overall choice. I therefore shift my provisional recommendation to Candidate\u202fC, pending any additional insights on adaptability or feedback orientation."}
